class.description:
[TextInsertionValues] holds values for placeholders such as [code]{game_name}[/code] or [code]{max_level}[/code]. Edit [member values] in the inspector as a table of names and values, save the resource as [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code] and add it with [method TextInsertionServer.add_values], or list it in [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/text_insertion/default_values] to add it at startup.
Several resources can be added at once, for example one for the base game and one per DLC or mod. The resource with the higher [member priority] wins when several have the same name.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var values = TextInsertionValues.new()
values.set_value(&"game_name", "Star Harbor")
TextInsertionServer.add_values(values)

# Values from a JSON file.
values.values = JSON.parse_string(FileAccess.get_file_as_string("res://data/names.json"))
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var values = new TextInsertionValues();
values.SetValue("game_name", "Star Harbor");
TextInsertionServer.AddValues(values);

// Values from a JSON file.
var data = Json.ParseString(FileAccess.GetFileAsString("res://data/names.json")).AsGodotDictionary();
foreach (var entry in data)
{
	values.SetValue(entry.Key.AsStringName(), entry.Value);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] Resources hold values only, no code. Change them on the main thread.
